  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-800 mt-8 mb-4">7. WHAT RIGHTS YOU HAVE</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>IN SHORT:</strong> You have certain rights with respect to your and/or your child's personal data that
    we collect and process.
  </p>
  <p>
    You have a variety of rights granted to you pursuant to GDPR. Below we outline the main of them in brief albeit
    there are others that we did not list. Should you need more detailed guidance, please contact us, our
    representative or independent GDPR specialist on your rights.
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
    <li>
      <strong>Right of consent withdrawal.</strong> You have the right to withdraw from us your consent to process
      your and/or your child's personal data at any time. The withdrawal of consent shall not affect the lawfulness
      of processing based on consent before its withdrawal.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right of access.</strong> You have the right to obtain from us confirmation as to whether your and/or
      your child's personal data are being processed, and, where that is the case, access to that personal data, the
      information concerning how we process it and some other information.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to rectification.</strong> You have the right to obtain from us the rectification of inaccurate
      your and/or your child's personal data. You also have the right to have incomplete personal data completed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to erasure ('right to be forgotten').</strong> You have the right to obtain from us the erasure
      of your and/or your child's personal data, and we will erase that personal data without undue delay.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to restriction of processing.</strong> You have the right to ask us to restrict processing your
      and/or your child's personal data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to object.</strong> You have the right to object on grounds relating to your particular
      situation to processing of your and/or your child's personal data and we will no longer process that personal
      data unless we are able to demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds for such processing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to data portability.</strong> You have the right to receive from us your and/or your child's
      personal data which you have provided to us in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format and
      have the right to transmit those data to another controller.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Right to lodge a complaint.</strong> You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
      authority, in particular, in the member EU state of your habitual residence, place of work or of an alleged
      infringement of the GDPR, about our collection and processing of your and/or your child's personal data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    You can always manage the privacy of your and/or your child's personal data by updating your privacy settings,
    by managing marketing and promotional communications from us or changing your browser settings to opt-out of
    cookies in your browser settings (if you however disallow some or all of the cookies, the Services may not work).
  </p>
  <p>
    We respond to all requests we receive from individuals in the EEA that are using the Services directed to the
    EEA wishing to exercise their data protection rights in accordance with applicable data protection laws.
